.TH QDOCK-SERVER 1 "September 2026" "0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
qdock-server \- authenticated TCP server for Quansheng observations and controls
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B qdock-server
.RI "--serial device | --replay file " [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Publishes JSON observations over TCP using the qdock-lan/1 protocol.
Serial acquisition is shared among clients. Controls require explicit options.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --help
Show all supported options and their current defaults.
.TP
.BI "--serial " device
Use the specified serial device; read-only unless an optional query/control is enabled.
.TP
.BI "--replay " file
Replay a regular capture file without opening a serial device.
.TP
.BI "--seconds " number
Limit serial acquisition duration (default 15 seconds, maximum 86400).
.TP
.BI "--listen " address
Local listening address (default 127.0.0.1).
.TP
.BI "--port " number
TCP port (default 8765).
.TP
.B --allow-ptt
Allow momentary PTT for an authenticated, subscribed LAN client.
.TP
.BI "--ptt-max-seconds " number
Maximum PTT duration, 1 to 180 seconds (default 60). Requires --allow-ptt.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B QDOCK_LAN_TOKEN
Required authentication token, 16 to 256 UTF-8 bytes.
.SH NOTES
PTT is released on lease expiry, owner disconnect or orderly shutdown.
A broken serial link or forced process termination can prevent delivery of release.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR qdock-server-gui (1),
.BR qdock-probe (1)
.PP
.I /usr/share/doc/qdock-server/LAN_PROTOCOL.md
